  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Sometimes when debugging networked behavior it can be easier to set up a complex reproduction case, then build and test multiple times into the same instance to update debug logic. With the current behavior, when you hit 'build and test' to launch a new build with a new client, all existing clients also rejoin - and end up in a different instance than the new one that you just launched.\nWhile this behavior can be useful in some cases, having a way to disable it would also be helpful depending on the specific things you're trying to debug.",
